---
source: tests/compliance_snapshots.rs
---
{
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "sbom-tools",
          "version": "[VERSION]",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/sbom-tool/sbom-tools",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-4",
              "name": "BsiTr03183FormatEligibility",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 v2.1.0 §4: Newly generated/updated SBOMs must be CycloneDX 1.6+ or SPDX 3.0.1+"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 v2.1.0 §4: Newly generated/updated SBOMs must be CycloneDX 1.6+ or SPDX 3.0.1+. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §4; BSI TR-03183-2: §7."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Regenerate the SBOM as CycloneDX 1.6+ or SPDX 3.0.1+ in JSON or XML. TR-03183-2 v2.1.0 §4 lists the eligible specifications for newly generated or updated SBOMs; the §7 transitional grace for the v2.0.0 minimums (CycloneDX 1.5 / SPDX 2.2.1) ended 2026-02-20.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §4 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §7 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Regenerate the SBOM as CycloneDX 1.6+ or SPDX 3.0.1+ in JSON or XML. TR-03183-2 v2.1.0 §4 lists the eligible specifications for newly generated or updated SBOMs; the §7 transitional grace for the v2.0.0 minimums (CycloneDX 1.5 / SPDX 2.2.1) ended 2026-02-20.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §4](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §7](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-1",
              "name": "BsiTr03183SbomCreator",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.1: Creator of the SBOM (email, or URL if no email)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.1: Creator of the SBOM (email, or URL if no email). References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify the SBOM creator with an email address, or a URL (e.g. the creator's home page) if no email is available; generation tools do not count as the creator.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add metadata.authors[] (name, email) or metadata.manufacturer (name, contact[].email); metadata.tools entries do not count.\n- SPDX 2.x: add a creationInfo.creators[] entry such as \"Person: Jane Doe (jane@example.com)\" or \"Organization: Example Ltd (sbom@example.com)\"; Tool: entries do not count.\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.createdBy to a Person or Organization element that has a name; createdUsing tools do not count.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Identify the SBOM creator with an email address, or a URL (e.g. the creator's home page) if no email is available; generation tools do not count as the creator.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add metadata.authors\\[\\] (name, email) or metadata.manufacturer (name, contact\\[\\].email); metadata.tools entries do not count.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a creationInfo.creators\\[\\] entry such as \"Person: Jane Doe (jane@example.com)\" or \"Organization: Example Ltd (sbom@example.com)\"; Tool: entries do not count.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.createdBy to a Person or Organization element that has a name; createdUsing tools do not count.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-1-CONTACT",
              "name": "BsiTr03183SbomCreatorContact",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.1: SBOM creator must carry an email address or URL"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.1: SBOM creator must carry an email address or URL. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add an email address to the SBOM creator entry, or a URL (creator home page / project web page) when no email exists — a bare name does not satisfy §5.2.1.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add metadata.authors[].email, or a metadata.manufacturer contact[].email or url.\n- SPDX 2.x: append the address to the creationInfo.creators[] entry, e.g. \"Person: Jane Doe (jane@example.com)\".\n- SPDX 3.0: agent emails are not read, but a creationInfo.createdBy element whose name includes an email address or URL counts.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Add an email address to the SBOM creator entry, or a URL (creator home page / project web page) when no email exists — a bare name does not satisfy §5.2.1.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add metadata.authors\\[\\].email, or a metadata.manufacturer contact\\[\\].email or url.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** append the address to the creationInfo.creators\\[\\] entry, e.g. \"Person: Jane Doe (jane@example.com)\".\n- **SPDX 3.0:** agent emails are not read, but a creationInfo.createdBy element whose name includes an email address or URL counts.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-2",
              "name": "BsiTr03183Timestamp",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.1: Timestamp of the SBOM data compilation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.1: Timestamp of the SBOM data compilation. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add the date and time of the SBOM data compilation (UTC 'Zulu' timestamps recommended).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.timestamp (RFC 3339, e.g. 2026-01-15T10:00:00Z).\n- SPDX 2.x: set creationInfo.created (Created).\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.created on the SpdxDocument.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Add the date and time of the SBOM data compilation (UTC 'Zulu' timestamps recommended).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.timestamp (RFC 3339, e.g. 2026-01-15T10:00:00Z).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set creationInfo.created (Created).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.created on the SpdxDocument.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-3",
              "name": "BsiTr03183ComponentName",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Component name (fallback: actual filename)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Component name (fallback: actual filename). References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Name every component. When the component creator assigned no name, the actual filename MUST be used instead.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].name.\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].name (PackageName), or files[].fileName for files.\n- SPDX 3.0: set name on the element.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Name every component. When the component creator assigned no name, the actual filename MUST be used instead.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].name.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].name (PackageName), or files\\[\\].fileName for files.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set name on the element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-VERSION",
              "name": "BsiTr03183ComponentVersion",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Component version (fallback: RFC 3339 modification date)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Component version (fallback: RFC 3339 modification date). References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Version every component (SemVer/CalVer recommended). When no version is assigned, the modification date of the file as RFC 3339 date-time MUST be used instead.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].version.\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].versionInfo (PackageVersion).\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageVersion on the package.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Version every component (SemVer/CalVer recommended). When no version is assigned, the modification date of the file as RFC 3339 date-time MUST be used instead.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].version.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].versionInfo (PackageVersion).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageVersion on the package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-INVENTORY",
              "name": "BsiTr03183Inventory",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: SBOM lists at least one component"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: SBOM lists at least one component. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "List the software components the product is made of. A document with no components, or with only files, snippets or cryptographic assets, is not a software inventory; validate a CBOM with --standard cnsa2 or pqc instead.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component and list the components in components[].\n- SPDX 2.x: list the packages in packages[] and name the product in documentDescribes.\n- SPDX 3.0: add software_Package elements and set the SpdxDocument's rootElement to the product package.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "List the software components the product is made of. A document with no components, or with only files, snippets or cryptographic assets, is not a software inventory; validate a CBOM with --standard cnsa2 or pqc instead.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component and list the components in components\\[\\].\n- **SPDX 2.x:** list the packages in packages\\[\\] and name the product in documentDescribes.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add software\\_Package elements and set the SpdxDocument's rootElement to the product package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-LICENSE",
              "name": "BsiTr03183DistributionLicence",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Distribution licence(s) per component"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Distribution licence(s) per component. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2; BSI TR-03183-2: §6.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare the distribution licence(s) of every component, named by SPDX licence identifier or expression (§6.1).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add components[].licenses[] entries (license.id with an SPDX identifier, or an expression).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].licenseDeclared (PackageLicenseDeclared) or packages[].licenseConcluded; NOASSERTION and NONE are read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: add a hasDeclaredLicense (or hasConcludedLicense) Relationship from the package to a simplelicensing_LicenseExpression element.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §6.1 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Declare the distribution licence(s) of every component, named by SPDX licence identifier or expression (§6.1).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add components\\[\\].licenses\\[\\] entries (license.id with an SPDX identifier, or an expression).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].licenseDeclared (PackageLicenseDeclared) or packages\\[\\].licenseConcluded; NOASSERTION and NONE are read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add a hasDeclaredLicense (or hasConcludedLicense) Relationship from the package to a simplelicensing\\_LicenseExpression element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §6.1](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-LICENSE-SPDX",
              "name": "BsiTr03183SpdxLicenceNaming",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §6.1: Licences must be named by SPDX identifier/expression"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §6.1: Licences must be named by SPDX identifier/expression. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §6.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Name licences by SPDX identifier or expression; consult Scancode LicenseDB (LicenseRef-scancode-*) or use LicenseRef-<entity>-* for unlisted licences. Licence text MUST NOT be used as a substitute for an identifier.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §6.1 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Name licences by SPDX identifier or expression; consult Scancode LicenseDB (LicenseRef-scancode-\\*) or use LicenseRef-\\<entity\\>-\\* for unlisted licences. Licence text MUST NOT be used as a substitute for an identifier.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §6.1](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-CREATOR",
              "name": "BsiTr03183ComponentCreator",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Component creator (email, or URL if no email)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Component creator (email, or URL if no email). References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Record the component creator: the email address (or URL if no email) of the entity that created or maintains the component.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors[].name).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages[].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Record the component creator: the email address (or URL if no email) of the entity that created or maintains the component.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors\\[\\].name).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages\\[\\].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-4",
              "name": "BsiTr03183ComponentHash",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Hash of the deployable component as SHA-512"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Hash of the deployable component as SHA-512. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Provide the hash of the deployed/deployable component as SHA-512 — §5.2.2 names the algorithm, so SHA-256 or other algorithms alone do not satisfy the required field (additional hashes may coexist).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add a components[].hashes[] entry with alg SHA-512.\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].checksums[] entry with algorithm SHA512 (PackageChecksum: SHA512: <value>).\n- SPDX 3.0: add a verifiedUsing[] Hash entry with algorithm sha512.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Provide the hash of the deployed/deployable component as SHA-512 — §5.2.2 names the algorithm, so SHA-256 or other algorithms alone do not satisfy the required field (additional hashes may coexist).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add a components\\[\\].hashes\\[\\] entry with alg SHA-512.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].checksums\\[\\] entry with algorithm SHA512 (PackageChecksum: SHA512: \\<value\\>).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add a verifiedUsing\\[\\] Hash entry with algorithm sha512.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-4-MISSING",
              "name": "BsiTr03183ComponentHashMissing",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2/§3.2.1: Component has no hash of the deployable form"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2/§3.2.1: Component has no hash of the deployable form. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2; BSI TR-03183-2: §3.2.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add a SHA-512 hash of the deployable component. §3.2.1 permits omission only when the information cannot exist due to the way the component is assembled (e.g. logical components).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add a components[].hashes[] entry with alg SHA-512.\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].checksums[] entry with algorithm SHA512 (PackageChecksum: SHA512: <value>).\n- SPDX 3.0: add a verifiedUsing[] Hash entry with algorithm sha512.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §3.2.1 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Add a SHA-512 hash of the deployable component. §3.2.1 permits omission only when the information cannot exist due to the way the component is assembled (e.g. logical components).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add a components\\[\\].hashes\\[\\] entry with alg SHA-512.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].checksums\\[\\] entry with algorithm SHA512 (PackageChecksum: SHA512: \\<value\\>).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add a verifiedUsing\\[\\] Hash entry with algorithm sha512.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §3.2.1](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-5",
              "name": "BsiTr03183Dependencies",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Dependencies on other components"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Dependencies on other components. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Enumerate all direct dependencies of each component.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add dependencies[] entries (ref plus dependsOn[]); an entry with an empty dependsOn records a component that has no dependencies.\n- SPDX 2.x: add relationships[] entries such as DEPENDS_ON (or DEPENDENCY_OF, CONTAINS) between the packages.\n- SPDX 3.0: add Relationship elements with relationshipType dependsOn (or contains) between the packages.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Enumerate all direct dependencies of each component.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add dependencies\\[\\] entries (ref plus dependsOn\\[\\]); an entry with an empty dependsOn records a component that has no dependencies.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add relationships\\[\\] entries such as DEPENDS\\_ON (or DEPENDENCY\\_OF, CONTAINS) between the packages.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add Relationship elements with relationshipType dependsOn (or contains) between the packages.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-5-COMPLETENESS",
              "name": "BsiTr03183DependencyCompleteness",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Completeness of the dependency enumeration must be clearly indicated"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Completeness of the dependency enumeration must be clearly indicated. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Clearly indicate the completeness of the dependency enumeration (complete or incomplete).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set compositions[].aggregate (complete, incomplete, incomplete_first_party_only, …); the first composition is read.\n- SPDX 2.x: no field records completeness.\n- SPDX 3.0: set completeness (complete or incomplete) on the dependsOn Relationship elements.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Clearly indicate the completeness of the dependency enumeration (complete or incomplete).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set compositions\\[\\].aggregate (complete, incomplete, incomplete\\_first\\_party\\_only, …); the first composition is read.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no field records completeness.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set completeness (complete or incomplete) on the dependsOn Relationship elements.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-2-4",
              "name": "BsiTr03183UniqueIdentifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.4: Other unique identifiers (purl/CPE) — additional tier"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.4: Other unique identifiers (purl/CPE) — additional tier. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add unique identifiers (purl, CPE) to components. §5.2.4 is the additional tier: the field MUST be provided when an identifier exists for the component.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].purl (or cpe, or swhid[]).\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory PACKAGE-MANAGER, referenceType purl and a pkg: locator (or a SECURITY cpe23Type, or a PERSISTENT-ID swh entry).\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageUrl, or add an externalIdentifier[] entry with externalIdentifierType packageUrl, cpe23, swhid or swid.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.4 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Add unique identifiers (purl, CPE) to components. §5.2.4 is the additional tier: the field MUST be provided when an identifier exists for the component.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].purl (or cpe, or swhid\\[\\]).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory PACKAGE-MANAGER, referenceType purl and a pkg: locator (or a SECURITY cpe23Type, or a PERSISTENT-ID swh entry).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageUrl, or add an externalIdentifier\\[\\] entry with externalIdentifierType packageUrl, cpe23, swhid or swid.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.4](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-3-1",
              "name": "BsiTr03183NoVulnerabilityInfo",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §3.1: An SBOM must not contain vulnerability information"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §3.1: An SBOM must not contain vulnerability information. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §3.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Remove vulnerability information from the SBOM and publish it separately (e.g. as CSAF advisories); a document containing both SBOM and vulnerability information does not conform to TR-03183-2.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: remove the vulnerabilities[] array.\n- SPDX 2.x: documents in this format carry no vulnerability data, so these entries were attached by enrichment.\n- SPDX 3.0: remove the security_Vulnerability elements and their affects and assessment Relationships.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §3.1 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Remove vulnerability information from the SBOM and publish it separately (e.g. as CSAF advisories); a document containing both SBOM and vulnerability information does not conform to TR-03183-2.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** remove the vulnerabilities\\[\\] array.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** documents in this format carry no vulnerability data, so these entries were attached by enrichment.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** remove the security\\_Vulnerability elements and their affects and assessment Relationships.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §3.1](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EO14028-TIMESTAMP",
              "name": "Eo14028Timestamp",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: SBOM creation timestamp (NTIA baseline)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: SBOM creation timestamp (NTIA baseline). References: EO 14028 §4; NTIA: Timestamp."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460",
              "help": {
                "text": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.timestamp (RFC 3339, e.g. 2026-01-15T10:00:00Z).\n- SPDX 2.x: set creationInfo.created (Created).\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.created on the SpdxDocument.\n\nReferences:\n- EO 14028 §4 (https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460)\n- NTIA: Timestamp (https://www.ntia.gov/report/2021/minimum-elements-software-bill-materials-sbom)",
                "markdown": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.timestamp (RFC 3339, e.g. 2026-01-15T10:00:00Z).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set creationInfo.created (Created).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.created on the SpdxDocument.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EO 14028 §4](<https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460>)\n- [NTIA: Timestamp](<https://www.ntia.gov/report/2021/minimum-elements-software-bill-materials-sbom>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EO14028-NAME",
              "name": "Eo14028ComponentName",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Component name (NTIA baseline)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Component name (NTIA baseline). References: EO 14028 §4; NTIA: Component Name."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460",
              "help": {
                "text": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].name.\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].name (PackageName), or files[].fileName for files.\n- SPDX 3.0: set name on the element.\n\nReferences:\n- EO 14028 §4 (https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460)\n- NTIA: Component Name (https://www.ntia.gov/report/2021/minimum-elements-software-bill-materials-sbom)",
                "markdown": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].name.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].name (PackageName), or files\\[\\].fileName for files.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set name on the element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EO 14028 §4](<https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460>)\n- [NTIA: Component Name](<https://www.ntia.gov/report/2021/minimum-elements-software-bill-materials-sbom>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EO14028-FORMAT",
              "name": "Eo14028MachineReadable",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Machine-readable SBOM format"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Machine-readable SBOM format. References: EO 14028 §4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460",
              "help": {
                "text": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\nReferences:\n- EO 14028 §4 (https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460)",
                "markdown": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EO 14028 §4](<https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EO14028-AUTOGEN",
              "name": "Eo14028AutoGeneration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Automated SBOM generation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Automated SBOM generation. References: EO 14028 §4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460",
              "help": {
                "text": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add metadata.tools with the tool's name and version.\n- SPDX 2.x: add a creationInfo.creators[] entry \"Tool: <name>-<version>\".\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.createdUsing to a Tool element whose name includes the version.\n\nReferences:\n- EO 14028 §4 (https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460)",
                "markdown": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add metadata.tools with the tool's name and version.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a creationInfo.creators\\[\\] entry \"Tool: \\<name\\>-\\<version\\>\".\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.createdUsing to a Tool element whose name includes the version.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EO 14028 §4](<https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EO14028-CREATOR",
              "name": "Eo14028Creator",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: SBOM creator identification"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: SBOM creator identification. References: EO 14028 §4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460",
              "help": {
                "text": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add metadata.authors[] (name, email), metadata.manufacturer or metadata.tools.\n- SPDX 2.x: add creationInfo.creators[] entries such as \"Organization: Example Ltd (sbom@example.com)\" or \"Tool: generator-1.0\".\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.createdBy to a Person or Organization element, or createdUsing to a Tool element.\n\nReferences:\n- EO 14028 §4 (https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460)",
                "markdown": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add metadata.authors\\[\\] (name, email), metadata.manufacturer or metadata.tools.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add creationInfo.creators\\[\\] entries such as \"Organization: Example Ltd (sbom@example.com)\" or \"Tool: generator-1.0\".\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.createdBy to a Person or Organization element, or createdUsing to a Tool element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EO 14028 §4](<https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EO14028-IDENTIFIER",
              "name": "Eo14028Identifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Component unique identification"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Component unique identification. References: EO 14028 §4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460",
              "help": {
                "text": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].purl (or cpe, or swhid[]).\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory PACKAGE-MANAGER, referenceType purl and a pkg: locator (or a SECURITY cpe23Type, or a PERSISTENT-ID swh entry).\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageUrl, or add an externalIdentifier[] entry with externalIdentifierType packageUrl, cpe23, swhid or swid.\n\nReferences:\n- EO 14028 §4 (https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460)",
                "markdown": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].purl (or cpe, or swhid\\[\\]).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory PACKAGE-MANAGER, referenceType purl and a pkg: locator (or a SECURITY cpe23Type, or a PERSISTENT-ID swh entry).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageUrl, or add an externalIdentifier\\[\\] entry with externalIdentifierType packageUrl, cpe23, swhid or swid.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EO 14028 §4](<https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EO14028-DEPENDENCY",
              "name": "Eo14028Dependency",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Dependency relationship information"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Dependency relationship information. References: EO 14028 §4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460",
              "help": {
                "text": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add dependencies[] entries (ref plus dependsOn[]); an entry with an empty dependsOn records a component that has no dependencies.\n- SPDX 2.x: add relationships[] entries such as DEPENDS_ON (or DEPENDENCY_OF, CONTAINS) between the packages.\n- SPDX 3.0: add Relationship elements with relationshipType dependsOn (or contains) between the packages.\n\nReferences:\n- EO 14028 §4 (https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460)",
                "markdown": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add dependencies\\[\\] entries (ref plus dependsOn\\[\\]); an entry with an empty dependsOn records a component that has no dependencies.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add relationships\\[\\] entries such as DEPENDS\\_ON (or DEPENDENCY\\_OF, CONTAINS) between the packages.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add Relationship elements with relationshipType dependsOn (or contains) between the packages.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EO 14028 §4](<https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EO14028-VERSION",
              "name": "Eo14028Version",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Component version information"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Component version information. References: EO 14028 §4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460",
              "help": {
                "text": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].version.\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].versionInfo (PackageVersion).\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageVersion on the package.\n\nReferences:\n- EO 14028 §4 (https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460)",
                "markdown": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].version.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].versionInfo (PackageVersion).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageVersion on the package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EO 14028 §4](<https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EO14028-INTEGRITY",
              "name": "Eo14028Integrity",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Component integrity verification (hashes)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Component integrity verification (hashes). References: EO 14028 §4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460",
              "help": {
                "text": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add components[].hashes[] entries with alg SHA-256, SHA-384 or SHA-512 and the content.\n- SPDX 2.x: add packages[].checksums[] entries with algorithm SHA256, SHA384 or SHA512 and the checksumValue (PackageChecksum).\n- SPDX 3.0: add verifiedUsing[] Hash entries with algorithm sha256, sha384 or sha512 and the hashValue.\n\nReferences:\n- EO 14028 §4 (https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460)",
                "markdown": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add components\\[\\].hashes\\[\\] entries with alg SHA-256, SHA-384 or SHA-512 and the content.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add packages\\[\\].checksums\\[\\] entries with algorithm SHA256, SHA384 or SHA512 and the checksumValue (PackageChecksum).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add verifiedUsing\\[\\] Hash entries with algorithm sha256, sha384 or sha512 and the hashValue.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EO 14028 §4](<https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EO14028-DISCLOSURE",
              "name": "Eo14028Disclosure",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e)(viii) practice: Vulnerability disclosure program"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e)(viii) practice: Vulnerability disclosure program. References: EO 14028 §4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460",
              "help": {
                "text": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add a metadata.component.externalReferences[] entry of type security-contact (or advisories).\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory SECURITY and referenceType advisory (or url) to the described package.\n- SPDX 3.0: add an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType securityAdvisory to the root package.\n\nReferences:\n- EO 14028 §4 (https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460)",
                "markdown": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add a metadata.component.externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type security-contact (or advisories).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory SECURITY and referenceType advisory (or url) to the described package.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType securityAdvisory to the root package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EO 14028 §4](<https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EO14028-SUPPLIER",
              "name": "Eo14028Supplier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Supplier identification"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: Supplier identification. References: EO 14028 §4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460",
              "help": {
                "text": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors[].name).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages[].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\nReferences:\n- EO 14028 §4 (https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460)",
                "markdown": "Follow the SBOM practice of EO 14028 §4(e): use a machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.2+, or SPDX 3.0+), generate the SBOM with a tool, and include unique identifiers, versions, hashes, dependencies and supplier information. This is practice, not a federal mandate: OMB M-26-05 rescinded the M-22-18 attestation requirement, though an agency may still ask for an SBOM in its contract.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors\\[\\].name).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages\\[\\].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EO 14028 §4](<https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EO14028-INVENTORY",
              "name": "Eo14028Inventory",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: SBOM lists the software's components"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EO 14028 §4(e) practice: SBOM lists the software's components. References: EO 14028 §4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460",
              "help": {
                "text": "List the software components the product is made of. A document with no components, or with only files, snippets or cryptographic assets, is not a software inventory; validate a CBOM with --standard cnsa2 or pqc instead.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component and list the components in components[].\n- SPDX 2.x: list the packages in packages[] and name the product in documentDescribes.\n- SPDX 3.0: add software_Package elements and set the SpdxDocument's rootElement to the product package.\n\nReferences:\n- EO 14028 §4 (https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460)",
                "markdown": "List the software components the product is made of. A document with no components, or with only files, snippets or cryptographic assets, is not a software inventory; validate a CBOM with --standard cnsa2 or pqc instead.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component and list the components in components\\[\\].\n- **SPDX 2.x:** list the packages in packages\\[\\] and name the product in documentDescribes.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add software\\_Package elements and set the SpdxDocument's rootElement to the product package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EO 14028 §4](<https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2021-10460>)"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
